      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Durable state is memory for the orchestrator: run envelopes, epochs, claims, checkpoints, events, facts, and artifacts preserve scheduling truth between processes. This page defines the run lifecycle and event boundaries, then the execution and knowledge records beneath them."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-the-section-separates-th-2": {
      "id": "b-index-the-section-separates-th-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The section separates the durable record model, run control, and scheduler wake-up protocol so each contract has one home. Read the pages in order to move from stored scheduling truth, through run transitions and recovery, to event handling."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
